Title:
bloodhound-ldapx.py (BloodHound.py CE ingestor with ldapx obfuscation, pacing, and resume)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
This repository is a modified BloodHound.py Community Edition (CE) Python ingestor designed for red team OPSEC during Active Directory enumeration. It routes LDAP/GC queries through a managed `ldapx` proxy that rewrites LDAP search filters, attribute lists, and base DNs to obfuscate collection patterns while still returning correct results. It adds granular rate controls for LDAP searches vs paged results, plus separate throttling for host-based SMB/RPC collection methods (sessions, local admin, RDP/DCOM/PSRemote, etc.). The tool supports DC-only collection through SOCKS5 (including Kerberos TCP/88) to avoid direct DC connectivity and to simplify proxying without `proxychains`. It can partition large LDAP searches into `objectGUID` slices and resume interrupted runs safely using checkpointing and atomic JSON writes. Output is BloodHound CE-compatible JSON/ZIP, making it useful for red teams/pentesters operating in monitored environments with LDAP query-rate or detection controls.

Technical Focus:
- LDAP query obfuscation via ldapx middleware (filter/attrlist/baseDN rewriting)
- LDAP/GC collection pacing (intervals + jitter) and host RPC throttling
- Kerberos authentication reuse (ccache/TGT/service tickets) and SOCKS5 routing
- LDAPS channel binding/signing handling via TLS + injected channel binding
- Large-directory enumeration via `objectGUID` partitioning and paging control
- Resumable collection with checkpoints and safe/atomic JSON output

Use Cases:
- OPSEC-focused BloodHound CE data collection in monitored AD environments
- Running DC-only enumeration through a SOCKS pivot without direct DC access
- Avoiding LDAP query-rate threshold alerts by trickling searches/pages
- Long-running collections in large domains with crash-safe resume capability
- Obfuscating LDAP query signatures to reduce straightforward detection based on filters/attributes

Keywords:
BloodHound.py, BloodHound CE, Active Directory, LDAP, Global Catalog, ldapx, LDAP obfuscation, LDAPS, channel binding, LDAP signing, Kerberos, ccache, TGT, service ticket, SOCKS5, Impacket, paging cookie, member;range, SMB, RPC, session enumeration, local admin enumeration, objectGUID partitioning, resume checkpoint, JSON ingestor